    "function": "contrast",
    "source_turn_preview_server_only": "Trees do more than cast shadows. Their leaves transfer water into the atmosphere, which can cool the surrounding air when moisture evaporates. This process is called transpiration. However, trees require suitable soil and water; planting them into tiny sealed pits may keep them alive without providing much cooling. The lesson is to plan for roots, not just branches."
